## SQ-CNS-01 | Comfort / Nourishment split at startup
@group A
@commands Boot 2: `grep -iE "damage tag\|damage_tags\|creativeengineering:(fire\|magic\|burn_tick)" logs/latest.log`; with `[damage_tags]` logging on, set the bot on fire and hit it with an Instant Damage potion, read the `DamageTagLogger` lines
@pass Damage tags load from `creativecommon` (32 plus CD's `creativedelight:stoves`), no unknown `#creativeengineering:` reference; the fire hit is tagged `fire`/`burn_tick`, the magic hit `magic`
@fails A file still naming `#creativeengineering:`: grep `development/*/src/main/resources/data/*/damage_tags`
@from batches/r1102b/s1_A.qb
bootexpect \[comfort_nourishment\] \d+ ruled foods set, \d+ bottles stripped, \d+ other foods lost Nourishment
bootreject \[comfort_nourishment\] (could not read|no item_dict key)
bootreject comfort_nourishment\.js.*(Error|error|exception)
shell grep -o "\[comfort_nourishment\] [0-9]* ruled foods set.*" logs/latest.log | head -1
look the ruled count is 269 (row text) or the current comfort_nourishment.json count

## SQ-CNS-02 | Comfort / Nourishment on eight foods
@group A
@commands Same boot: `/execute if block <glass> #creativecommon:wthit/needs_silk_touch` on a placed glass block; `grep -iE "jei_order_tags\|wthittags" logs/kubejs/server.log`
@pass Glass matches; both scripts load with no error
@fails `wthittags.js` TAG strings, `jei_order.js` TAG_ROOT
@from batches/r1102b/s1_R.qb
> zq food farmersdelight:noodle_soup
> zq food farmersdelight:beef_stew
> zq food farmersdelight:bone_broth
> zq food farmersdelight:dog_food
> zq food minecraft:golden_carrot
> zq food minecraft:enchanted_golden_apple
> zq food delightful:chunkwich
> zq food delightful:azalea_tea
expect food farmersdelight:noodle_soup: .*farmersdelight:nourishment amp 0 4800t
expect food farmersdelight:beef_stew: .*farmersdelight:comfort amp 0 4800t
reject food farmersdelight:bone_broth: .*(comfort|nourishment)
expect food farmersdelight:dog_food: .*farmersdelight:comfort amp 0 1200t
expect food minecraft:golden_carrot: .*farmersdelight:nourishment amp 0 2400t
expect food minecraft:enchanted_golden_apple: .*farmersdelight:nourishment amp 0 4800t
expect food minecraft:enchanted_golden_apple: .*minecraft:absorption
reject food delightful:chunkwich: .*nourishment
reject food delightful:azalea_tea: .*(comfort|nourishment)
reject not a food|\[zq\] error

## SQ-CNS-03 | Comfort / Nourishment on cans match their dishes
@group A
@commands Boot 2 then boot 3: `grep -iE "item merge\|swap_merges" logs/latest.log` each time
@pass Boot 2 runs the merge rewrite once (stamp `creativecommon:swap_merges`); boot 3 skips it
@fails `swap/ItemMerges` STAMP
@from batches/r1103/sB_2.qb
> zq food farmersdelight:noodle_soup
> zq food creativeengineering:canned_noodle_soup
> zq food creativeengineering:canned_bone_broth
> zq food farmersdelight:beef_stew
> zq food creativeengineering:canned_beef_stew
waitlog \[zq\] food creativeengineering:canned_beef_stew: 30
expect \[zq\] food creativeengineering:canned_noodle_soup: .*farmersdelight:nourishment
reject \[zq\] food creativeengineering:canned_bone_broth: .*farmersdelight:(nourishment|comfort)
expect \[zq\] food creativeengineering:canned_beef_stew: .*farmersdelight:comfort
reject (Unknown (item|block|entity)|Unknown or incomplete command|Incorrect argument for command|not a food|\[(zq|zsb|zlbs)\] (error|unknown))
look the canned noodle soup's nourishment ticks equal the noodle soup's; the canned beef stew's comfort ticks equal the beef stew's

## SQ-CNS-04 | no Compat / CD / Common mixin failures; Curios hands, face, feet slots registered by Equipment
@group A
@commands Same boot: `grep -E "creativecompat.mixins.json\|creativedelight.mixins.json\|creativecommon.mixins.json" logs/latest.log \| grep -iE "fail\|error\|could not"`; `/curios list @p` (or the Curios screen on the bot)
@pass No mixin failures (Compat's Jetpack and falling-block mixins, CD's two Central Kitchen mixins on the client config only); the hands, face and feet slots exist (now registered by Equipment)
@fails Equipment constructor `CuriosSlots::enqueue` under the `curios` check
@from batches/r1113/c2_a1.qb
bootreject (creativecompat|creativedelight|creativecommon)\.mixins\.json.*(rror|ailed|could not)
> curios list c2b
sleep 2
> curios list
expect (?i)hands
expect (?i)face
expect (?i)feet
look the curios list output names the slot types hands, face and feet (registered by Equipment)

## SQ-CNS-05 | Common's JFR events (creativecommon.ServerTick, LevelTick) are recorded
@group A
@commands Short JFR recording on boot 2 (perf suite settings, `server/perf/ce-server.jfc`), then `java tools/perf/PerfParse.java <file>`
@pass `creativecommon.ServerTick` and `creativecommon.LevelTick` events counted
@fails `PerfJfrEvents` names, the parser's prefix
@from batches/r1113/c2_a1.qb
shell for p in $(pgrep -x java); do [ "$(readlink /proc/$p/cwd)" = "$PWD" ] && jcmd $p JFR.dump name=ce filename=$PWD/perf/c2_cns05.jfr 2>&1 | tail -1; done; ls -la perf/c2_cns05.jfr 2>&1 | tail -1
shell rm -rf perf/c2_cns05_parse; java $INST/tools/perf/PerfParse.java perf/c2_cns05_parse perf/c2_cns05.jfr 2>&1 | tail -3; grep -c '"creativecommon.ServerTick"' perf/c2_cns05_parse/events.jsonl; grep -c '"creativecommon.LevelTick"' perf/c2_cns05_parse/events.jsonl
look both counts above 0 (event type names as written in events.jsonl; if both 0, grep the file for "creativecommon." to see the real names before calling FAIL). If no JFR (CE_PERF=0 at setup) the dump line says no recording: not judged

